@1 = ~Party Stash: one infinite stash shared by the whole party (requires EEex). Before uninstalling: Ctrl + left click on the weight bag to empty the stash~
@2 = ~Requires EEex.~
@3 = ~Stash~
@4 = ~Every character carries it so the game counts what is inside as carried (quests). The whole party's shared stash, on the inventory page. Click an item to take it; Shift + double-click a backpack item or press Space (Store all) to store; Ctrl + click marks an item to sell with the merchant's "Sell Marked" button. A bag put in the stash is emptied into it and kept in the Bags tab: stash items it can hold weigh nothing. The rest counts against the sum of the members' weight allowances; above it, everyone is slowed down.~
@5 = ~Sorted loot: on the ground, in containers and in the loot bar~
@6 = ~Baldur's Gate 1 look (recommended)~
@7 = ~Baldur's Gate II look (recommended)~
@8 = ~Party Stash: before uninstalling, empty the stash in game: Ctrl + left click on the big bag next to the weight, on the inventory page. Your collected bags come back filled with the items they can hold; everything else drops on the ground. Otherwise the stash contents stay in your saves but cannot be reached until the mod is reinstalled.~
@9 = ~Baldur's Gate 1 look~
@10 = ~Baldur's Gate II look~
@11 = ~Party Stash: one infinite stash shared by the whole party (requires EEex). Before uninstalling: Ctrl + left click on the weight bag to empty the stash~
@12 = ~For Baldur's Gate: Enhanced Edition only.~
@13 = ~For Baldur's Gate II: Enhanced Edition / EET only.~
